    longDescription: "The Amsterdam to Dubai route connects Schiphol Airport (AMS) — one of Europe's largest hubs — with Dubai International Airport (DXB), the world's busiest international airport by passenger traffic. Four carriers operate this corridor: KLM and Emirates offer daily nonstop service, while Etihad and Transavia provide additional options depending on season. With multiple daily departures, travelers can almost always find a flight that fits their schedule.\\n\\nNonstop flights take 6 hours 25 minutes to 6 hours 35 minutes and cover 5,230 km (3,250 miles). Emirates and KLM operate the majority of nonstop seats, with Etihad routing via Abu Dhabi (AUH) and Transavia offering seasonal low-cost nonstop service. For most travelers, nonstop is worth the premium — the connecting alternatives add 3 to 6 hours of travel time.\\n\\nPricing varies sharply by season. The cheapest months to fly are January, February, and October, when round-trip economy fares can drop to $250-$320 on Transavia or Etihad. The most expensive periods are the December holiday season and the late-March to early-April spring break, when fares climb above $600. Booking 4-8 weeks ahead typically secures the best average price; Tuesday departures are consistently 10-20% cheaper than Friday or Sunday flights.\\n\\nAirline comparison:\\n- Emirates: full-service, daily nonstop, best for comfort and A380 experience, includes meals and 30kg baggage.\\n- KLM: full-service home carrier at Schiphol, daily nonstop, reliable European service, includes meals and checked baggage.\\n- Etihad: routes via Abu Dhabi (1 stop), often cheapest, includes baggage on most fares.\\n- Transavia: low-cost, seasonal nonstop, lowest base fares but charges for baggage and seat selection.\\n\\nDubai International Airport (DXB) is a world-class hub with three terminals, extensive duty-free, lounges, and fast connections to downtown Dubai via the Metro (Red Line, ~20 minutes to Deira). Terminal 1 serves most European carriers; Emirates uses Terminal 3. Visa requirements depend on nationality — many passport holders can obtain a visa on arrival or an e-visa in advance through the UAE immigration portal; check before travel as rules change.\\n\\nFor the best deal, compare all four carriers on Flighko, set a price alert for your travel dates, and consider flying Tuesday or Wednesday. If flexibility allows, October offers the deepest discounts outside holiday periods.",
