    description: "Looking for cheap flights from Bangkok to Singapore? Compare prices across 5 airlines including Bangkok Airways, AirAsia, Thai Airways, Scoot, and Vietjet. Flight ticket from Bangkok to Singapore starts at $80 round trip. Bangkok to Singapore flight time is just 2 hours 15 minutes to 2 hours 25 minutes, covering 1,416 km. Book 3-6 weeks ahead for the best prices.",
    seoTitle: "Bangkok to Singapore Flights from $80 | Compare Cheap Deals",
    seoDescription: "Find Bangkok to Singapore flights from $120 round trip. Compare cheap fares, airlines, travel days, and real-time deals to save more with Flighko.",
    h1: "Bangkok to Singapore Flights",
    longDescription: "The Bangkok to Singapore route is a high-frequency corridor connecting two of Southeast Asia's most vibrant cities. With five airlines operating nonstop services, travelers have options ranging from full-service carriers like Thai Airways and Bangkok Airways to ultra-budget choices like AirAsia, Scoot, and Vietjet. This route sees over 30 daily departures, making it easy to find a flight that fits your schedule.\\n\\nBangkok's Suvarnabhumi Airport (BKK) is Thailand's main international hub, offering extensive duty-free shopping, lounges, and dining. Singapore's Changi Airport (SIN) consistently ranks among the world's best airports, featuring the Jewel Changi complex with its indoor waterfall, free movie theaters, and butterfly garden — perfect for transit passengers.\\n\\nThe cheapest month to fly from Bangkok to Singapore is October, when round-trip fares can drop below $80 on budget carriers. December and January see the highest prices due to holiday demand from both Thai and Singaporean travelers. For the best average prices, book your flight 4-8 weeks before departure and aim for a Tuesday departure, which is typically 15-20% cheaper than weekend flights.\\n\\nSingapore offers visa-free entry for most nationalities for up to 90 days, making it an accessible destination. The local currency is the Singapore Dollar (SGD), and while Singapore is known for being expensive, hawker centers serve meals from just SGD $3–$5. English is the primary language, so communication is effortless for most international travelers.\\n\\nFor travelers on a budget, AirAsia and Vietjet offer the lowest fares but charge extra for baggage and meals. Thai Airways and Bangkok Airways include checked baggage and meals in the ticket price, making them better value for travelers with luggage. Scoot occupies the middle ground with competitive base fares and optional ScootPlus upgrades for extra legroom and meals.",
