      { question: "What is the flight time from Chicago to Las Vegas?", answer: "Nonstop flights from Chicago O'Hare (ORD) to Las Vegas (LAS) take approximately 3 hours 30 minutes to 4 hours, covering ~1,530 km (950 miles). United, American, Southwest, and Delta operate frequent nonstop service." },
      { question: "Which airlines fly nonstop from Chicago to Las Vegas?", answer: "United (from ORD), American (from ORD/DFW), Southwest (from MDW/MDW), and Delta (from ORD/ATL) all offer daily nonstop ORD-LAS service. Budget carriers like Spirit and Frontier also fly the route with connections via Denver or Dallas." },
      { question: "What is the cheapest month to fly Chicago to Las Vegas?", answer: "August and September are typically the cheapest months — round-trip fares from $180 on Southwest/Spirit. December and February (presidents week) are most expensive ($280-$350). Tuesday and Wednesday departures usually offer the best rates." },
      { question: "How much are flights from Chicago to Las Vegas right now?", answer: "Currently $190-$280 round trip on Southwest/Spirit/Frontier. United and American typically $250-$380. Prices shift daily — book 2-4 weeks ahead and fly mid-week for best value. Set a Flighko price alert." },
      { question: "Is it cheaper to fly from Chicago O'Hare or Midway to Las Vegas?", answer: "Southwest flies exclusively from Midway (MDW) with fares from $180 round trip. O'Hare (ORD) has more carrier options (United, American, Delta) but often $50-$100 higher. If Southwest flies your dates, MDW is usually cheaper; otherwise ORD has more schedule flexibility." },
      { question: "Do I need a visa for Las Vegas from Chicago?", answer: "No visa required — Las Vegas is domestic travel for US citizens. Valid government-issued ID (driver's license or state ID) is sufficient for airport security. International travelers need standard US entry documentation." },
