    seoDescription: "Singapore to Bangkok flights from $80 round trip on 5 nonstop airlines (SQ, TG, AirAsia, Scoot, Jetstar). 2h 15m flight. Cheapest month (Sep), visa-free entry, baggage guide — 2026 update.",
    longDescription: "The Singapore to Bangkok route is one of the busiest air corridors in Southeast Asia, connecting two of the region's most visited cities. With five airlines offering nonstop service, travelers have excellent options ranging from full-service carriers like Singapore Airlines and Thai Airways to budget-friendly choices like AirAsia and Scoot.\n\nSingapore Changi Airport (SIN) consistently ranks among the world's best airports, offering excellent lounges, dining, and transit facilities. Bangkok's Suvarnabhumi Airport (BKK) is the main international gateway, connected to the city center by the Airport Rail Link (45 minutes, 45 THB), taxis (approximately 300 THB), and ride-hailing apps like Grab.\n\nThe cheapest month to fly from Singapore to Bangkok is September, when round-trip fares can drop below $100 on budget carriers. December and January see the highest prices due to holiday demand. For the best average prices, book your flight 3-6 weeks before departure and aim for a Tuesday departure, which is typically 15-20% cheaper than Friday flights.\n\nThailand offers visa-free entry for most nationalities (30-day exemption), making this a hassle-free destination. The local currency is the Thai Baht (THB), and your Singapore dollars go a long way here — a street food meal costs 40-60 THB ($1.50–$2), while a taxi across central Bangkok runs 150-250 THB ($4–$7).\n\nFor travelers on a budget, AirAsia and Scoot offer the lowest fares but charge extra for baggage and meals. Singapore Airlines and Thai Airways include checked baggage and meals in the ticket price, making them better value for travelers with luggage. Jetstar offers a middle ground with competitive base fares and optional add-ons.",
